    "role": "student",
    "content": "Okay, I see what you're pointing out. Besides `a`, the variable `y` is also being read on the right-hand side of the line `a = a + y`. \n\nIf we were attempting to use pass-by-result, `y` would be uninitialized at the start of the function. This would mean that `y` would contain garbage data, and using it in the calculation would lead to unpredictable and incorrect results. It's essentially the same issue as trying to use `a` before initialization – both parameters are uninitialized when the function begins."
  }
]
```

